    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nREA MURPHY introduces this particularly solid family home to the open market for immediate sale. Spacious rooms throughout and a valuable 20ft x 20ft workshop complimented with extensive parking space and particularly mature grounds. Located just off the N81, north of Baltinglass, the property enjoys easy access to West Dublin and County Kildare employment centres. \n\nRecessed a considerable distance from the public road, the 1950's bungalow is nestled behind mature shrubbery and established boundaries. The Residence was extended in 1988 and now offers 3 large Double Bedrooms, 2 Bathrooms, a beautiful Lounge, a very functional living room linking into the fully fitted Kitchen. Sprinkled with relics from former years, first impressions to refurbish the Residence throughout may be re-thought towards enhancing the character of this sturdy home. Outside, the sizable workshop space is a real bonus and the quality tarmacadam finish to the driveway and parking area is low maintenance. The established trees and shrubbery shelter belt provides total privacy from the public road and there is more than sufficient lawn area on this 2/3 acre site for family enjoyment. The distance of the residence from the public road and the established site boundaries makes this property ideally suited to the younger family.\n\nThe immediate location has a quantity of quality one-off housing with a strong sense of community connected to both Stratford-on-Slaney village and the Glen of Imaal communities. Local primary schools at Donoughmore and Stratford-on-Slaney, Secondary School bus passes the door and plenty of outdoor activities with the local GAA Clubs, walking routes, nearby Golf Clubs and the outdoor activity centre in Baltinglass.\n\nRecent refurbishment works completed include both Bathrooms, internal insulation, electrical upgrades with supporting certification, new water well pump along with a new oil burner. Internally the Residence is presented in good liveable condition suitable for immediate occupation. The Residence offers the option of removing carpets and stripping back the raised timber floors for an enhanced appearance, and enhancing the character of this appealing family home. The AGA cooker is a gem - ideal for slow cooking. The AGA will also delivers domestic hotwater and an ambient heat for the whole house. Throughout the house there is a genuine good vibe of the property having been a cherished family home for many years. The practial layout of the main Living / Kitchen area connecting to the garage workshop with both served with the adjacent shower room, all close to the rear access is just a small indicator of the practical appeal of this property. Now available for immediate purchase, there is an opportunity for the genuine Buyer looking to settle in this rural setting - accessible to West Dublin (40 minutes), but nicely removed from the everyday bussle to allow one enjoy the country feeling.\n\nContact REA Murphy for a viewing appointment.\n\n \n\nACCOMMODATION:\n\nEntrance Hall.\n\nLounge.\n\nBathroom.\n\n3 Bedrooms all Double.\n\nLiving room.\n\nKitchen with Dining area.\n\nRear Hall with W.C.\n\nGarage.\n\nSOME DIGITALISED ENHANCED PHOTOGRAPHS ARE INCLUDED TO HIGHLIGHT THE POTENTAIL OF THE ACCOMMODATION.\n\nOUTSIDE:\n\n0.66ac plot with front and side gardens. Tarmacadam drive and ample parking space.\n\n \n\nSERVICES:\n\nPrivate Sewerage system. Private water system. Electricity connected. Excellent broadband options available.\n\n \n\nTRANSPORT:\n\nBlessington 24Km Baltinglass 6.50Km \n\n132 Bus Eireann route on the N81. \n\n885 Local Link route from Stratford to Sallins train Station via Blessington and Naas.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Appealing 1950's residence oozing with character and standing on very private grounds.\nSpacious rooms throughout, with tow living areas and a valuable workshop attached.\nRural location yet close to the N81 route to Dublin City and to local primary school options (2 within 2.50Km) \nBeautiful grounds with mature trees and shrubbery and a rural setting ideal for country walks and a relaxed country living.\nSelection of sports clubs and outdoor activities close by including horse riding, golf, GAA, mountain bike trails and kayaking \nCity West - 45Km Blessington - 25Km Naas - 30Km Baltinglass - 7Km"
      },
